  "conclusion_review": {
    "recommended_wording": "Across this exploratory 300-query source-domain pilot, a fixed top-1 disagreement gate skipped 83 of 300 cross-encoder invocations (27.7%) and scored 4,340 rather than 6,000 candidate pairs. nDCG@10 point estimates were 0.5019 gated versus 0.4986 always-on; the paired 95% query-bootstrap difference interval [-0.00583, 0.01283] includes zero. Recall@10 fell from 0.6323 hybrid to 0.6173 gated. These are observed pilot tradeoffs, not proof of improved primary-metric performance, statistical equivalence, unseen-family generalization, or deployed latency gains.",
    "unsupported_claims": [
      "statistically significant nDCG improvement",
      "statistical equivalence or proven quality preservation",
      "measured adaptive end-to-end speedup",
      "unseen API-family generalization",
      "novel trained adaptive gate"
    ]
